.TH CLOG_SET_FACILITY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
clog_set_facility \- change the syslog facility
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/clogger.h>

ccol_retval_t clog_set_facility(clog logger,
                                clog_syslog_facility_t facility);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Sets the syslog facility that the shared backing store holds.  The
facility goes into the PRI field of every RFC 5424 message, as
(facility * 8) + severity.  The value lives on the shared store, so the
change is visible to every logger handle that writes to the same file
descriptor, the root logger and every derived logger.

The facility matters only when the output format is CLOG_FMT_SYSLOG.
Calling this with any other format does no harm: the store keeps the new
value, and it reaches the output once somebody selects CLOG_FMT_SYSLOG.

Available facility codes (RFC 5424 / RFC 3164):
  CLOG_SYSLOG_KERN     (0): kernel messages
  CLOG_SYSLOG_USER     (1): user-level messages (default)
  CLOG_SYSLOG_MAIL     (2): mail system
  CLOG_SYSLOG_DAEMON   (3): system daemons
  CLOG_SYSLOG_AUTH     (4): security / authorization messages
  CLOG_SYSLOG_SYSLOG   (5): internal syslogd messages
  CLOG_SYSLOG_LPR      (6): line printer subsystem
  CLOG_SYSLOG_NEWS     (7): network news subsystem
  CLOG_SYSLOG_UUCP     (8): UUCP subsystem
  CLOG_SYSLOG_CRON     (9): clock daemon
  CLOG_SYSLOG_AUTHPRIV (10): security / authorization (private)
  CLOG_SYSLOG_FTP      (11): FTP daemon
  CLOG_SYSLOG_LOCAL0   (16): local use 0
  ...
  CLOG_SYSLOG_LOCAL7   (23): local use 7
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
logger    Logger handle.
facility  The facility code to use (clog_syslog_facility_t).  A value
          that the enum does not name (12 to 15, or anything outside
          0 to 23, such as 99 or -1) is refused and the facility stays
          as it is, which keeps the PRI of every record in the range
          0 to 191 that RFC 5424 allows.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success       The facility is set.
ccol_invalid_args  clog_syslog_facility_t does not name facility.  The
                   facility stays as it is.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Thread-safe, because the mutex of the shared backing store protects the
call.
The default facility is CLOG_SYSLOG_USER.
Asserts when logger is CLOG_NULL, stale or already closed.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clog_get_facility (3),
.BR clog_set_format (3)
